{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/251175-fate-brandings-something-different-for-fate-itself","id":251175,"title":"Fate Brandings: Something different for Fate itself","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-06T18:15:38-07:00","id":251175,"title":"Fate Brandings: Something different for Fate itself","content":"Something I've begun cobbling together. It's not much, but its a first attempt at possible house rule for how Fate Bindings will work in any of my future Scion games. Comments and suggestions are more than welcome as I mostly just threw this together as a rough draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","user":"Gemstone","date":".  Butchered Link 09-07-2014, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T10:35:01-07:00","id":251549,"title":"","content":"I just noticed that the Forum butchers my link so the actual page doesn't display <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> the link to the mechanic is <a href=\"http://tideofthunder.wikia.com/wiki/Fate_Branding_(Scion\" target=\"_blank\">http://tideofthunder.wikia.com/wiki/...randing_(Scion</a>)<br /> <br /> Okay, the forum hates my wikia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Well, just add a ) at the end if the page isn't displayed so it reads Fate_Branding_(Scion)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T04:44:18-07:00","id":253994,"title":"","content":"I've gone over this a few times and I have to say that I really like the idea. I haven't playtested it, as I'm in the middle of a game and I think this should best be used in a new game, but I really like not only the way that Fate actually has some meaning at Hero level but also that it can just keep getting worse and worse. I mean if you rescue someone who's fallen out of a building and you get a Brand over it, it's only going to make things easier for you to do it again, which risks you getting more caught up in things.<br /> <br /> Which leads, really, to needing to rescue people all the time. And instead of the bad-ass giant slayer you really want to be, what Fate slots you in as is the new God of Accidents. You walk down a street and you got people toppling out of buildings left right and centre <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I kind of like that Fate could have that kind of derailing effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T05:18:20-07:00","id":254016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/251175-fate-brandings-something-different-for-fate-itself?p=253994#post253994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've gone over this a few times and I have to say that I really like the idea. I haven't playtested it, as I'm in the middle of a game and I think this should best be used in a new game, but I really like not only the way that Fate actually has some meaning at Hero level but also that it can just keep getting worse and worse. I mean if you rescue someone who's fallen out of a building and you get a Brand over it, it's only going to make things easier for you to do it again, which risks you getting more caught up in things.<br /> <br /> Which leads, really, to needing to rescue people all the time. And instead of the bad-ass giant slayer you really want to be, what Fate slots you in as is the new God of Accidents. You walk down a street and you got people toppling out of buildings left right and centre <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I kind of like that Fate could have that kind of derailing effect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was kinda the effect I was aiming for when i wrote Brandings. I will try to straighten up the text as soon as I've had a decent 8 hours of sleep and not running solely on coffe ^^ I will also add some suggestions on how to remove brandings. Difficult, even for gods, but not impossible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/593-gemstone","name":"Gemstone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}